import{_ as e,o as a,c as t,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const m=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 924 | Myriad-Rank Republican Civilizational Charter · Article 23 | Protection of Myriad-Rank Culture","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 924 | Myriad-Rank Republican Civilizational Charter · Article 23 | Protection of Myriad-Rank Culture","no":924,"module":5,"tags":["Charter","Article 23","Cultural Protection","Diversity","Civilizational Autonomy"],"related":["52-Alien-Race Classification and Symbiosis","05-Myriad-Ranks Co-Advancement Basic Program","35-Developing Catch-Up Civilizations"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0924_模块5-第二十三条-万族文化保护.md","filePath":"en/0924_模块5-第二十三条-万族文化保护.md"}'),o={name:"en/0924_模块5-第二十三条-万族文化保护.md"};function r(s,i,l,c,u,d){return a(),t("div",null,[...i[0]||(i[0]=[n('<h1 id="entry-924-myriad-rank-republican-civilizational-charter-·-article-23-protection-of-myriad-rank-culture" tabindex="-1">Entry 924 | Myriad-Rank Republican Civilizational Charter · Article 23 | Protection of Myriad-Rank Culture <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-924-myriad-rank-republican-civilizational-charter-·-article-23-protection-of-myriad-rank-culture" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 924 | Myriad-Rank Republican Civilizational Charter · Article 23 | Protection of Myriad-Rank Culture&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 5 · Civilization Final-Finalization Canonical Entries | Benchmark base: Documents 52, 05, 35</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-symbiosis-is-not-assimilation" tabindex="-1">Introduction: symbiosis is not assimilation <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-symbiosis-is-not-assimilation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: symbiosis is not assimilation&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Myriad-Rank republicanism pursues common evolution, but common evolution is not melting Myriad Ranks into one shape. Article 23 stipulates protection of Myriad-Rank culture: every clan&#39;s and plane&#39;s unique culture, beliefs, lifestyles, and aesthetic traditions are all charter-protected; forced assimilation under the names of &quot;advanced,&quot; &quot;unified,&quot; or &quot;efficiency&quot; is prohibited. The Anchor Symbiotic Civilization wants Myriad Ranks&#39; symbiosis and common prosperity, not Myriad Ranks&#39; uniformity. Diversity itself is civilization&#39;s wealth.</p><p>This article is from beginning to end placed under the six top-level axioms — the anti-predation axiom draws the bottom line, the republican axiom of Myriad Races establishes the subject, the collective-ascension axiom sets the direction, the causal self-discipline axiom guards the boundary, the law-first axiom preserves self-consistency; the five together constitute this article&#39;s insurmountable spiritual boundary.</p><p>Together with the previous five axioms, this article is also bound by Axiom 6 · Universal Equal Infinite Law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing and layabouts retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will not be eliminated by the times; strivers and Youth Supremes may superimpose more and higher levels of infinity; predation thus fundamentally loses meaning.</p><h2 id="i-jurisprudential-basis" tabindex="-1">I. Jurisprudential Basis <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-jurisprudential-basis" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Jurisprudential Basis&quot;">​</a></h2><p>This article is based on the Alien-Race Classification and Symbiosis (Document 52), the Myriad-Ranks Co-Advancement Basic Program (Document 05), and the &quot;autonomy-and-co-governance-combined principle&quot; (Document 03). Its jurisprudence is: the republican axiom of Myriad Races includes not only equal evolutionary right, but also the equal right to preserve one&#39;s own culture. Forced assimilation is just like predation — both are the strong imposing their own standards on others. Cultural diversity also provides civilization with more evolutionary possibilities; a homogenized civilization&#39;s risk-resistance is far below a plural civilization&#39;s.</p><h2 id="ii-normative-content-four-bottom-lines-of-cultural-protection" tabindex="-1">II. Normative Content: Four Bottom Lines of Cultural Protection <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-normative-content-four-bottom-lines-of-cultural-protection" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Normative Content: Four Bottom Lines of Cultural Protection&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Article 23 draws cultural protection&#39;s boundaries:</p><ol><li><strong>Autonomy right</strong>: each clan, without violating the charter, enjoys autonomy over internal culture, institutions, and customs;</li><li><strong>No forced assimilation</strong>: prohibited to require alien clans to abandon their culture or adopt other clans&#39; lifestyles on any grounds;</li><li><strong>Record and transmission</strong>: each clan&#39;s cultural classics, crafts, and traditions are archived and protected by the Alaya Network, preventing loss;</li><li><strong>Free cross-boundary exchange</strong>: clans may voluntarily exchange, draw on, and merge culture, but merging must be voluntary and may not be imposed.</li></ol><h2 id="iii-scope" tabindex="-1">III. Scope <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-scope" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Scope&quot;">​</a></h2><p>This article applies to all clans and planes joining Myriad-Rank republicanism. It especially protects weak, young, small-population clans — these clans&#39; cultures are most easily diluted by strong civilizations. This article does not protect bad customs that &quot;in the name of culture actually predate&quot;: if some clan&#39;s customs include human sacrifice, enslavement, or predatory cultivation, that bad custom is not culturally protected and is handled under Article 1.</p><h2 id="iv-consequences-of-violation" tabindex="-1">IV. Consequences of Violation <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-consequences-of-violation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Consequences of Violation&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Forced assimilation, banning alien languages and customs, using cultural-superiority theory to marginalize weak clans, destroying alien cultural classics, all constitute unconstitutionality under this article. Consequences: relevant policies are revoked, damaged cultural records are restored through Alaya archives; those under the name of &quot;cultural purification&quot; actually running clan oppression are pursued heavily under anti-predation and anti-discrimination.</p><h2 id="v-supervision-mechanism" tabindex="-1">V. Supervision Mechanism <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-supervision-mechanism" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Supervision Mechanism&quot;">​</a></h2><p>This article is executed by the cultural archive library within Alaya Network + multi-layer supervision: each clan&#39;s cultural classics are fully archived, and loss risk automatically alerts; the Anchor Supervisory Committee monitors each clan&#39;s cultural survival state, discovering some clan&#39;s culture systematically suppressed immediately intervenes; each clan retains the right to sue the Symbiotic Court for cultural assimilation.</p><h2 id="vi-an-odd-flower-in-a-hundred-flower-garden" tabindex="-1">VI. An Odd Flower in a Hundred-Flower Garden <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-an-odd-flower-in-a-hundred-flower-garden" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. An Odd Flower in a Hundred-Flower Garden&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Article 23 makes Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s Myriad-Rank symbiosis like a hundred-flower garden, not a uniform lawn. A clan from a cold plane preserves its unique culture of ice-carved narratives; a consciousness-information clan continues its poems transmitted only in dreams. No one forces assimilation because they differ from the mainstream; their classics are archived by the Alaya Network, and loss risk automatically alerts. Civilization thus gains countless ways of seeing the world, and risk-resistance also strengthens. True confidence never fears others being different; symbiosis&#39;s highest realm is precisely letting Myriad Ranks stand side by side, yet each beautiful, each appreciating the other.</p><h2 id="vii-axiom-6-s-projection-in-cultural-protection" tabindex="-1">VII. Axiom 6&#39;s Projection in Cultural Protection <a class="header-anchor" href="#vii-axiom-6-s-projection-in-cultural-protection" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VII. Axiom 6&#39;s Projection in Cultural Protection&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The universal equal infinite law adds another bottom line to cultural protection: regardless of whether a clan&#39;s culture flourishes or declines, the basic infinite power inherent in each of its members does not increase or decrease because of it. No matter how niche or obscure a culture, its bearers still retain floor infinity, and are not judged eliminable because of a small clan. Cultural protection is thus not only an aesthetic choice, but also a solemn recognition of every ordinary being&#39;s inherent infinity.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><p><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: wiping out one culture wipes out one unique way of seeing the world; this article preserves this cognitive diversity</p></li><li><p><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: cultural assimilation is a form of spiritual predation; this article positively prohibits it</p></li><li><p><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang-Luo-type civilizations take the strong&#39;s culture as the only standard; Heng Yuan Zhou protects Myriad-Rank cultural diversity, each enjoying its own beauty</p></li><li><p><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: from large clans to small clans, culture is uniformly protected</p></li><li><p><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: every new civilization accepted has its culture brought under protection; the civilizational hundred-flower garden blooms ever fuller</p></li><li><p><strong>Universal equal infinity</strong>: every being inherently possesses basic infinite power; the easygoing layabouts retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will not be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes may superimpose higher-level infinity; predation thus fundamentally loses meaning</p></li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Protection of Myriad-Rank culture is the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization&#39;s maturity marker. A truly powerful civilization does not fear others being different, but takes pride in others being different. Symbiosis&#39;s highest realm is Myriad Ranks standing side by side, yet each beautiful.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/52-异族分类与共生.html">Entry 52 · Alien-Race Classification and Symbiosis</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/05-万族共进基本纲领.html">Entry 05 · Myriad-Ranks Co-Advancement Basic Program</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/35-发展中赶超型文明.html">Entry 35 · Developing Catch-Up Civilizations</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/903_模块5-第二条-万族平等进化权.html">Entry 903 · Article 2 Myriad Ranks&#39; Equal Evolutionary Right</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',27)])])}const p=e(o,[["render",r]]);export{m as __pageData,p as default};
